WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.775
Messier 15 or M15 is a globular cluster in the constellation Pegasus.

00:06.276 --> 00:15.839
It was discovered by Jean-Dominique Maraldi in 1746 and included in Charles Messier's catalogue of comet-like objects in 1764.

00:16.480 --> 00:25.033
At an estimated 12.5±1.3 billion years old, it is one of the oldest known globular clusters.
